Bittle simulator artwork, revision 1

Source geometry: PetoiCamp/ros_opencat, ros1 commit
85962928970ee47f38d53cad56f8e304863a87f5, directory
petoi_ROS_model_docs/bittle_ros/bittle_description (meshes and URDF).
https://github.com/PetoiCamp/ros_opencat/tree/85962928970ee47f38d53cad56f8e304863a87f5/petoi_ROS_model_docs/bittle_ros/bittle_description
The package and repository each contain an MIT LICENSE (both reproduced below).

Changes: offline Blender/Cycles lighting, black/yellow materials, original
modeled double infrared board and lenses, standing/folded poses, and eight
illustrative gait frames. Accessory, rendering code and derived images are
provided under MIT with these source notices. Copyright (c) 2026 Neuraffica.
The generic Bittle mesh is used as the Bittle X exterior; internal electronics
are not represented. Joint poses illustrate simulator state, not measured
servo angles. No product photography, textures or HDRIs are redistributed.
Petoi and Bittle names/marks belong to their respective owners; no endorsement.

Visual reference only (not included in shipped assets):
https://www.petoi.com/products/petoi-robot-dog-bittle-x-voice-controlled
https://www.petoi.com/pages/bittle-smart-robot-dog-model-overview

Reproduction in the flybrain worktree:
  uv venv work/render-env --python 3.11
  uv pip install --python work/render-env/bin/python bpy==5.0.1 pillow==13.0.0
  python3 scripts/bittle-art/fetch.py
  work/render-env/bin/python scripts/bittle-art/render.py
  work/render-env/bin/python scripts/bittle-art/sync.py /absolute/path/to/synaptix-worktree

top.webp and side.webp are ten horizontal 384px tiles: stand, rest, then eight
phases. head.webp is a separate 384px layer with the neck pivot at (192,134.94).
Orthographic width is 32cm; +X on the model is forward. Top sensor origin is
(192,85.8). Side sensor x is 298.2; floor y is 360. Rendering parameters are
in scripts/bittle-art/render.py. The web simulator needs top/head only; side
is shipped there too to keep the artwork distribution identical.

flybrain is the artwork source of truth. sync.py regenerates manifest.json
(SHA-256 and bytes), copies all asset files into apps/web/public/bittle, and
updates the guide's embedded still. Commit both copies together after edits.
Assets load from the local demo server/site only when their view is drawn.

